cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this result, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Six AND Gates Beat Seven: A Counterexample to Quadratic-Circuit Optimality over F2"
abstract: >-
  An explicit homogeneous quadratic map Q: F2^6 -> F2^5 with multiplicative
  complexity 6 over XOR-AND circuits, while every quadratic (level-one) circuit
  for Q needs 7 AND gates. Both bounds are exact, proved by hand and confirmed
  by an exhaustive verifier. Research note; not peer-reviewed.
